{"content":{"activity_type":"event_msg/item_completed","completed_at_ms":1790216288634,"item":{"content":[{"text":"The project is healthy and essentially feature-complete for its current scope. I found no formal backlog or code-level TODOs.\n\n## Project snapshot\n\n`annals` is a small TypeScript/Node library extracted from `conversation-ledger`. It stores producer-defined events as canonical JSONL in git notes, anchored to the commit that was current when captured.\n\nThe main flow is:\n\n- Producers call `openLedger()` and `appendEvents()`.\n- Events are validated, deterministically identified, and redacted before writing.\n- Reads default to records reachable from `HEAD`.\n- A fetch refspec and pre-push hook synchronize notes.\n- Sync performs a secret scan before anything new is shared.\n- Re-anchor records preserve reachability after rebases and squash merges.\n- Namespaces let different producers maintain separate note refs and configuration.\n\nThe design boundary is unusually clear: annals owns storage, identity, redaction, reachability, and transport; producer packages own event meaning and payload validation.\n\nThe repository is very young—seven commits, all since September 1—and recent work has concentrated on extraction cleanup, namespace correctness, producer-neutral envelopes, fixture safety, and pre-push recursion prevention.\n\n## Current health\n\n- `main` is clean and exactly aligned with `origin/main`.\n- Build passes under Node 20+.\n- Tests: **151 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped** out of 152.\n- The skipped test is the optional `gitleaks` oracle because `gitleaks` is not installed; see [secret-corpus.test.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/src/test/secret-corpus.test.ts:139).\n- `npm pack --dry-run` succeeds and produces a sensible 91.5 KB package containing compiled JS, declarations, source maps, README, and license.\n- The public [GitHub repository](https://github.com/evintunador/annals) currently has [no open issues](https://github.com/evintunador/annals/issues), [no open pull requests](https://github.com/evintunador/annals/pulls), no tags, and [no releases](https://github.com/evintunador/annals/releases).\n- The npm registry returns `404` for `annals`; version `0.1.0` has not been published.\n\n## Remaining work\n\nThere are no confirmed functional TODOs. The remaining items are release/documentation polish:\n\n1. **Fix missing design-document references.** Three source headers point to `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md`, but no `docs/` directory exists:\n\n   - [known-secrets.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/src/redact/known-secrets.ts:3)\n   - [rules.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/src/redact/rules.ts:2)\n   - [scan.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/src/redact/scan.ts:2)\n\n   Either restore that design document or replace these references with durable documentation.\n\n2. **Add practical README usage.** The [README](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals/README.md:1) explains the architecture well, but contains no installation, library example, configuration reference, or test/development instructions. That is the largest usability gap before publishing.\n\n3. **Decide whether to release `0.1.0`.** The package metadata and tarball are ready, but npm publication, a git tag, and a GitHub release have not happened.\n\n4. **Add CI if this is becoming independently maintained.** There is no `.github/workflows` configuration, so the excellent test suite currently runs only when someone invokes it locally.\n\n5. **Run the optional external scanner before a release.** Installing `gitleaks` would exercise the one skipped compatibility test.\n\n6. **Optional extraction cleanup.** Several internal comments still say `cledger` or refer to `.cledger.json` even where the implementation is namespace-generic. Most are historical or illustrative rather than defects, but cleaning them up would make annals feel fully standalone.\n\nNo files were changed during this review.","type":"Text"}],"id":"msg_0a0adba4e6599070016ab488508e3487d2af27423cd7045e59","phase":"final_answer","type":"AgentMessage"},"started_at_ms":1790216272614,"thread_id":"01a0d131-8563-7453-ae36-468e6c8930b5","turn_id":"01a0d131-cbda-7161-9ba4-fdf8e878ea2d"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/annals","head":"d72d3aabee4777b77e270c19aabd61713ad891ce","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/annals.git"},"id":"ev2-e6c793ca8188b48261527b1d1948f97d83e0096997afd45a2c85e28b75ca5503","kind":"activity","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"01a0d131-8563-7453-ae36-468e6c8930b5","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-24T02:18:08.634Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"ordinal":116,"payload":{"completed_at_ms":1790216288634,"item":{"content":[{"text":"The project is healthy and essentially feature-complete for its current scope. I found no formal backlog or code-level TODOs.\n\n## Project snapshot\n\n`annals` is a small TypeScript/Node library extracted from `conversation-ledger`. It stores producer-defined events as canonical JSONL in git notes, anchored to the commit that was current when captured.\n\nThe main flow is:\n\n- Producers call `openLedger()` and `appendEvents()`.\n- Events are validated, deterministically identified, and redacted before writing.\n- Reads default to records reachable from `HEAD`.\n- A fetch refspec and pre-push hook synchronize notes.\n- Sync performs a secret scan before anything new is shared.\n- Re-anchor records preserve reachability after rebases and squash merges.\n- Namespaces let different producers maintain separate note refs and configuration.\n\nThe design boundary is unusually clear: annals owns storage, identity, redaction, reachability, and transport; producer packages own event meaning and payload validation.\n\nThe repository is very young—seven commits, all since September 1—and rece